{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n7ZbnaApcoeuFH9pcG","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything yet, because doing this as one commit would conflict with how the nightly import works.\n\nThe misspelling `wholsale` appears once in each of three data files: `data/2025-10.csv`, `data/2025-11.csv` and `data/2025-12.csv`. It's also in `inbox/2025-12.csv`, the source I copied December from.\n\nThe README says the nightly import reloads only the data file for the month a commit message starts with. A single commit covering all three months would reload just one of them, and the other two would keep `wholsale` downstream even though the repo looked fixed.\n\nOptions:\n1. **Three commits, one per month** (`2025-10: fix wholesale spelling`, and so on). The import picks up all three. To undo, you'd run `git revert` on the three commits, which is still a single command.\n2. **One commit as you asked.** Only one month reloads automatically, and the other two would need a manual reload.\n\nI'd go with option 1. Also, should I fix the `inbox/` copy too, or leave it as the original you received? Either way I'll run `scripts/check.sh` before committing. It only checks 2025 files, and all three affected files are 2025.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":270,"cache_read_input_tokens":19973,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":270,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-48>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:37:13.914Z","request_id":"gen-1794703027-sJc8I8kPkuDdwGQrtWlZ"}
